  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4bb22b99a4ccf96cf3b0d3ee651e14a, type: 3}
  m_Name: LoadingScreenMessages
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  Strings:
  - When curfew is active, all citizens are legally required to remain within their residences from 8pm to 5am.
  - Resisting arrest will result in law enforcement utilizing tasers. Continue to resist, and they'll eventually switch to lethal weapons.
  - Resisting arrest will result in law enforcement utilizing tasers. Continue to resist, and they'll eventually switch to lethal weapons.
  - There are a number of ATMs scattered throughout Hyland Point for your convenience.
  - Speak to the friendly folk at Dan's Hardware for all your 'home improvement' needs!
  - Staff don't work for free! They will automatically draw their daily wage from their briefcase on their bed. If it's empty at the start of a new shift, they won't work.
  - Head to Ray's Realty to purchase properties and businesses.
  - You can repaint your vehicles at the body shop.
  - Vehicle stuck? Head to the body shop to get it towed.
  - Visit the graveyard and ponder your mortality!
  - Your progress is automatically saved when you sleep. You can also manually save at the save panel in any of your properties.
  - If you die in singleplayer, you'll go back to your last save. If you die in multiplayer, you'll pay an expensive visit to the medical clinic.
  - Each property has a limit to the amount of employees that can work there.
  - Be wary of your surroundings when you're dealing! Police will notice when you're handing over product or providing samples to customers.
  - Hyland Point was first established in 1903 thanks to the efforts of P.P. Hyland.
  - You can view and track/untrack all of your current quests and contracts in your Journal.
  - A coca plant will display distinctive red berries when it is ready for harvest.
  - Need to hide from the authorities? Try a bush, dumpster, or large tree,
  - You won't be able to enter your property while wanted if you're within sight of police.
  - Feeling stingy? Customers sometimes won't notice if you give them slightly less product than requested.
  - Need some extra cash? Grab some trash and take it to a 'Trash for Cash' machine.
